      "text": "**Immediate action plan – scan, redact, and rewrite history**\n\n1. **Back up the repository**  \n   ```bash\n   git clone --mirror <repo-url> repo-backup.git\n   cd repo-backup.git\n   git bundle create ../repo-backup.bundle --all\n   ```\n   > Keeps a pristine snapshot in case something goes wrong.\n\n2. **Identify secrets** – run a proven scanner on the *working copy* first (no history rewrite yet).  \n   ```bash\n   # Install TruffleHog (Python) – works on files and commits\n   pip install trufflehog\n\n   # Scan latest tree (fast)\n   trufflehog filesystem --regex --entropy=True .\n\n   # Scan full history (slow, but catches old leaks)\n   trufflehog git file://$(pwd) --regex --entropy=True --since-commit=HEAD\n   ```\n   *Result*: a list of file‑path + commit‑hash + secret snippet.\n\n3. **Generate a redaction map**  \n   Create a JSON file `redact_map.json`:\n\n   ```json\n   {\n     \"path/to/file.py\": {\n       \"regex\": \"AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}\",\n       \"placeholder\": \"<AWS_ACCESS_KEY>\"\n     },\n     \"config.yml\": {\n       \"regex\": \"password:\\\\s*.+\",\n       \"placeholder\": \"password: <REDACTED>\"\n     }\n     // add entries from the TruffleHog output\n   }\n   ```\n\n4. **Rewrite history with `git filter-repo`** (recommended over BFG for fine‑grained control).  \n   Install:\n\n   ```bash\n   pip install git-filter-repo\n   ```\n\n   Run a one‑off rewrite that applies the map to **all** commits:\n\n   ```bash\n   # Bash helper to build a python “filter” script from the JSON map\n   cat > redact.py <<'EOF'\n   import json, re, sys\n   from pathlib import Path\n\n   # Load map\n   with open('redact_map.json') as f:\n       MAP = json.load(f)\n\n   def replace_content(blob):\n       path = blob.path.decode()\n       if path in MAP:\n           data = blob.data.decode(errors='ignore')\n           for entry in MAP[path].values():\n               pattern = re.compile(entry['regex'])\n               data = pattern.sub(entry['placeholder'], data)\n           blob.data = data.encode()\n       return blob\n\n   def filter_commit(commit, metadata):\n       # Apply to each file in the commit\n       for blob in commit.file_changes:\n           replace_content(blob)\n   EOF\n\n   # Execute the rewrite\n   git filter-repo --path-rename '' --replace-refs delete-no-add \\\n                  --commit-callback 'filter_commit' \\\n                  --blob-callback 'replace_content' \\\n                  --force\n   ```\n\n   *What it does*: walks every blob, matches the regexes from `redact_map.json`, substitutes the placeholder, and rewrites every commit that touched the file.\n\n5. **Validate the rewrite**  \n   ```bash\n   # Spot‑check a few known secret locations\n   git grep -E 'AKIA|password' --all\n   # Should return nothing\n   ```\n\n6. **Force‑push the cleaned history** (only if you control the repo and all collaborators can reset):\n\n   ```bash\n   git remote add origin <repo-url>\n   git push --force --all\n   git push --force --tags\n   ```\n\n   > **Critical**: inform every fork/clone to reclone or run `git fetch --all && git reset --hard origin/main`.\n\n7. **Add preventive controls**  \n   * Install a pre‑commit secret scanner (e.g., `detect-secrets`) to block future commits.  \n   * Add a CI step that runs TruffleHog on every PR.  \n   * Rotate any secrets that were exposed before the rewrite (you can’t guarantee old caches are clean).\n\n---\n\n### Minimal one‑liner for a quick‑and‑dirty fix (use only on a *single branch*, not full history)\n\nIf you just need to redact the current tip and are willing to keep the old commits (e.g., for a quick emergency patch):\n\n```bash\n# Replace in working tree\ngit ls-files -z | xargs -0 sed -i -E 's/AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}/<AWS_ACCESS_KEY>/g; s/password:\\s*.*/password: <REDACTED>/g'\n\ngit commit -am \"Redact exposed secrets (placeholder) – temporary fix\"\ngit push\n```\n\n> **Note**: This does *not* erase the secrets from history; run the full rewrite (steps 1–6) as soon as feasible.\n\n---\n\n### Checklist before you hit “push”\n\n- [ ] Backup verified (`repo-backup.bundle` exists).  \n- [ ] All secret regexes tested on a sample file.  \n- [ ] `git filter-repo` completed without errors.  \n- [ ] No secret strings appear in `git grep`.  \n- [ ] Team notified & instructed to reclone.  \n- [ ] Post‑commit CI secret scan enabled.  \n\nProceed with the rewrite, then lock down the pipeline to prevent recurrence. Let me know if you need a ready‑to‑run script that automates steps 2–5 for your repo.",
